**Theorem 8.2 (actual instruments for the entire exceptional segment).**
For every exceptional strength and every closed-interval parameter in
(CA.48), the following construction realizes its equality vector with
all the original five-mode, passive-reference and labelled-time
requirements.

Proof. Put $\tau=1/2+\theta$, $\lambda=1/2-\gamma\theta$.
Use the two supported high encoder products

$$
A_+=\sqrt\tau(\sqrt pD+\sqrt qT),\qquad
A_-=\sqrt{1-\tau}(\sqrt pD-\sqrt qT).
\tag{CA.55}
$$

They are assigned to their indicated binary records. Every nonzero one
has rank three: the determinant of the unweighted expression is
$\sqrt p\,h_0h_1h_2(p-\alpha q)
=\sqrt p\,h_0h_1h_2k>0$.
Use its three-dimensional output as the high carrier and the full
trace-preserving isometric live decoder $X\mapsto EXE^\dagger$.
The low supported products at record $+$ and $-$, respectively, are

$$
C_{+,\zeta}=\sqrt{\lambda/2}
 (\sqrt{1-p}D+\sqrt{1-q}T+\zeta S),\qquad
C_{-,\zeta}=\sqrt{(1-\lambda)/2}
 (\sqrt{1-p}D-\sqrt{1-q}T+\zeta S),\qquad \zeta=\pm1.
\tag{CA.56}
$$

Each nonzero product has rank two, since
$1-p=\alpha(1-q)+\beta$ and its $D$ coefficient is nonzero.
Apply the fixed range compression (CA.15) to each product $C=UR$:
encode by $R$ into a two-dimensional carrier, and use the full TP
isometric decoder $X\mapsto EUXU^\dagger E^\dagger$.
This gives exactly $CXC^\dagger$ on support after decoding.
Delete every zero-weight branch; this is required also at the interval
endpoints.

The two high coefficient matrices are exactly (CA.51), and the two
sign sums of low coefficient projectors are (CA.52).
The $S$ couplings cancel within each record. Their aggregate coefficient
sum is $I$, since its only candidate off-diagonal term is
$2\theta t-2\gamma\theta v=0$. The plus $DT$ entry is
$\tau t+\lambda v=s/2$, and its coordinate-$0$ effect is
$\tau\omega+\lambda(1-\omega)=1/2$.
Its remaining binary effect deficit is exactly $N_+$ in (CA.54).

For each record $r$ and each $i\in\{1,2\}$ with
$(N_r)_{ii}>0$, add a scalar encoder row
$\sqrt{(N_r)_{ii}}\langle i|$.
Its scalar decoder sends unit input into the complete failure measure
$w_jg(t)\,dt\,P_f$ at each original label $j$.
It is TP because $\sum_jw_j=1$ and
$\int_0^1g(t)\,dt=1$. The sum of these rows' effects at record $r$ is
$N_r$, and their forgotten failure measure is the prescribed supported
one because
$N_++N_-=M$. Thus the sum of supported joint effects is $I_V$, and
the record effects are $F_r^V$.

Precompose all these encoders with $E^\dagger$ on the full five-mode
input. At each record add the scalar complement map
$A\mapsto\operatorname{tr}(Q_5A)/2$, with the complete failure law
$g(t)\,dt\,P_f$ at original label $2$. Its effect is $Q_5/2$.
The total encoder effect is $I_5$, and the binary effects are exactly
$F_r$ on every input. Every cross-support block is annihilated;
unsupported sectors have exactly the required zero live action and
complement failure action. All the carrier decoders just specified are
TP on their full carrier matrix algebras, including scalar carriers.

The aggregate coefficient sum $I$ proves the full complex live channel
identity. The scalar effects and their specified decoders prove each
separate labelled Borel-time failure identity. These are identities of
linear completely positive maps, so tensoring them with the identity on
any passive reference proves the required reference identities, including
entangled, singular and subnormalized inputs. No reference is measured
or retained as payload. The failure law is a mathematical measure in the
instrument, subject to the native-clock boundary stated in §11.

At each record there are at most one high, two low, two scalar supported
failure, and one scalar complement branch: at most twelve in all.
Branch deletions reduce this number. All high acquisition mass is live;
its supported acquired effect is $G_\theta$. This proves sufficiency
for the whole segment, with no narrowing of Definition 2.3.
For nonexceptional strong strengths use (CA.44), and for weak strengths
use (CA.43). In particular all singleton cases are actually attained.
The conditioned live maps in (CA.55)--(CA.56) may vary with $\theta$;
the original specification fixes their forgotten sum and the binary
law, and permits precisely this freedom. $\square$

